etails on  this agreement is still a little bit  vague and the other matter that we  should be reminded horses this is more  austerity this is going to be  recessionary measures Greece's slip back  into recession the economy's expected  contract by at least three percent this  year and again in 2016 this  an economy that's already contracted by  morn the chords in the previous five  years so there's going to be tough  measures and there are certain issues  that had to be clear that one of the key  issues is the Greek banks which of  course since capital controls were  introduced at the start of July Greek  economy just got into three people Greek  savers have taken their money out from  the Greek banks and also non-performing  loans are skyrocketing as companies fall  further behind an individual's so the  banks have to be recapitalized it's  estimated they need something like 25  billion euros and also the whole big big  question about Greece's debt and whether  it's sustainable and I think the answer  that is the isn't people like the IMF  saying they won't come on board this new  bailout unless Greece's debt is made  sustainable and there's a certain amount  of resistance from the Germans on that  phone so a lot of hurdles from mr. to  you but I still a long way to go Philip  and I lost there in Athens
 

